# Copy to .env.submit in the project root (git-ignored) for `npm run submit`, or run
# `npx wxt submit init` to fill it interactively. In CI the same names are repository secrets.
# The stores' APIs only update existing items: create each listing once by hand first.
# Chrome needs 2-Step Verification on the Google account and API v2 cannot create items.
# Edge API keys expire. AMO needs 2FA on the Mozilla account before it issues keys.

# Chrome Web Store API v2: dashboard > Account > Publisher ID; item ID from the item's URL.
# Service account: https://developer.chrome.com/docs/webstore/using-api (API v1.1 shut down
# on 2026-10-15). Add the service account email under Dashboard > Account. Quote the private
# key and keep its \n escapes.
CHROME_API_VERSION=v2
CHROME_PUBLISHER_ID=
CHROME_EXTENSION_ID=
CHROME_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_CLIENT_EMAIL=
CHROME_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PRIVATE_KEY=

# Edge Partner Center > Microsoft Edge > Publish API (product ID from the extension overview).
EDGE_PRODUCT_ID=
EDGE_CLIENT_ID=
EDGE_API_KEY=

# AMO: https://addons.mozilla.org/developers/addon/api/key/
FIREFOX_EXTENSION_ID=magiclens@magiclens.dev
FIREFOX_JWT_ISSUER=
FIREFOX_JWT_SECRET=
